>> title: Roasted Beets
>> category: Vegetables & Sides
>> tags: beets, roast, vinegar, dill, side, make-ahead
>> counters: The Bowl Shop
>> aka: roasted beets, roast beetroot, oven beets, beetroot salad, dressed beets, baked beets
>> pairs-with: green-goddess-dressing, tabbouleh
>> servings: 6
>> time: 1 hr 40 min

>> step: The first hour is not roasting. It is steaming, in a foil tent, and that is why the skins come off in your hands.
The first hour is not roasting.

>> step: wash and cover with a splash of water
Scrub @beets{2%lb}(900 g; tops trimmed to an inch, tails left on) and put them in a baking dish with @water{1/4%cup}(60 mL) and @olive oil{1%Tbs}(15 mL), then cover the dish tightly with foil.

>> step: roast covered 400°F (200°C) 60 min
Roast @&(~1)covered beets{} at 400°F (200°C) ~roast{60%min}, until a paring knife slides to the middle and comes out with no resistance at all.

>> step: rub the skins off hot, under a towel
Rub the skins off @&(~1)hot beets{} with a folded towel you do not mind staining, then cut them into wedges.

>> step: dress while still warm
Toss @&(~1)peeled beets{} while still warm with @red wine vinegar{2%Tbs}(30 mL), @kosher salt{1%tsp} and @extra-virgin olive oil{2%Tbs}(30 mL).

>> step: stand 15 min, then fold in the herbs
Let @&(~1)dressed beets{} ~stand{15%min}, then fold in @dill{2%Tbs}(chopped) and @orange zest{1%tsp}.
